+- **set-gao-farmhouse.** Two unframed vignettes on one warm-paper ground: on the left, a farmhouse gate in an earthen wall at dusk, a heavy wooden bar across the doors, gray tile roofs, terraced fields behind; on the right, the front room inside, a square table laid with bowls of noodles, two oil lamps lit, plain wooden chairs, paper windows. Warm dusk gold outside, lamplight inside. Remove the plaque and every glyph-like stroke from the lintel; replace that area with one continuous strip of bare, unmarked dark timber while preserving the heavy horizontal gate bar as the location's primary marker. No signboard, inscription, seal, label, watermark, or decorative mark resembling writing may remain.
